        "title": "About US Primaries",
        "subject": "US Primaries",
        "summary": "U.S. primaries are state-administered elections held before the November general election to select or narrow the field of candidates for public office. The August 4, 2026 contests are part of the midterm-election cycle, but their rules and ballot formats differ by state.",
        "facts": [
          {
            "label": "Date and states",
            "value": "Kansas, Michigan, Missouri, Washington and Virginia hold 2026 primary elections on August 4; Arizona's 2026 primary was held earlier, on July 21.",
